{"id": "EUVD-2026-59362", "enisaUuid": "72df045f-50df-38c1-8c93-8154ba1229f3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: Fix dev use-after-free in xfrm async resumption\n\nxfrm async resumption hold skb->dev refcnt until after transport_finish.\nHowever, xfrm_rcv_cb may modify skb->dev to tunnel dev without taking\ndevice reference, such as vti_rcv_cb. The subsequent async resumption\nwill decrement the tunnel device's reference count, which lead to uaf\nof tunnel dev and refcnt leak of orig dev as below:\n\nunregister_netdevice: waiting for vti1 to become free. Usage count = -2\n\nStash the original skb->dev to fix refcnt imbalance. The new skb->dev set\nby xfrm_rcv_cb can race with device teardown. Extend rcu protection over\nxfrm_rcv_cb and transport_finish to prevent races.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:58", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fed4d3195a31125566876952ce66113ec1eb9008", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1acd93259b6be269e26be5d71c224bccd1f8352f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63a30015199912bd5055bead8001b1ae68a67cdb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8045c0df98d4f14c54e5cb875f1c9c0ce89fe4ff"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72463", "GHSA-23r2-6gqr-3m38"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "078b451f-e7cc-38a0-9e4f-29f8e1c4b35a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4236c30b437b80f673b9e08c8fae38b8d471ac9e <fed4d3195a31125566876952ce66113ec1eb9008"}, {"id": "0b440230-b181-33eb-ae40-7b24f00ed469", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19.13 <6.20"}, {"id": "226870b0-6db8-3070-b3cb-95d8a85340d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "302b8f85-5c81-35ff-b39e-864d65ede